WEBVTT

00:02.030 --> 00:03.480
Honestly...

00:03.860 --> 00:06.370
Taking in a monster?

00:06.370 --> 00:09.360
What in the world were you thinking?!

00:09.360 --> 00:14.690
Um, Miss Claire, it's not a monster 
anymore. It's a familiar.

00:14.690 --> 00:17.710
I was scared at first, too,

00:17.710 --> 00:19.870
but it's actually quite docile and cute.

00:19.870 --> 00:22.250
A monster is a monster!

00:22.250 --> 00:24.500
Have you forgotten the chaos 
we only just went through?

00:24.500 --> 00:28.140
But Ralaire is so sweet, Miss Claire!

00:28.690 --> 00:30.630
W-Wait just a minute.

00:30.630 --> 00:32.760
When you say "Ralaire," you don't mean...

00:32.760 --> 00:36.940
It's the slime's name. "Ralaire," 
from "Rae" and "Claire"!

00:37.930 --> 00:41.090
And just what are you doing using my name?!

00:41.090 --> 00:44.100
Don't say that! It's the fruit of our love!

00:44.450 --> 00:48.420
Forget it. I'll tell Mr. Torrid 
and have him kill it for me.

00:48.420 --> 00:49.220
Wha—

00:49.220 --> 00:51.130
Wait, Miss Claire!

00:51.130 --> 00:53.690
Ralaire is very clever! For real!

00:54.460 --> 00:55.420
Sit!

00:55.810 --> 00:56.740
Lay down!

00:57.280 --> 00:58.470
Turn around!

00:58.990 --> 01:00.360
See?

01:00.360 --> 01:02.620
It barely changed position at all!

01:02.620 --> 01:04.720
It needs to be done away with.

01:04.720 --> 01:06.580
Please wait, Miss Claire!

01:06.990 --> 01:09.920
No choice now! Ralaire, last resort time!

01:09.920 --> 01:11.320
Undine!

01:22.890 --> 01:25.660
Is that... me?

01:25.660 --> 01:30.620
Water slimes have a tendency to 
imitate any beautiful lady they see.

01:30.620 --> 01:32.270
I-Is that true?

01:32.270 --> 01:33.470
Yes!

01:33.470 --> 01:35.530
<i>But only half true.</i>

01:35.870 --> 01:38.780
<i>It's true that they mimic things around them.</i>

01:38.780 --> 01:42.140
<i>It's a type of camouflage 
they use to protect themselves.</i>

01:42.540 --> 01:46.540
<i>The part about beautiful ladies 
was a blatant lie, though.</i>

01:46.540 --> 01:51.580
Well, knowing that makes it... 
kind of cute, perhaps?

01:51.580 --> 01:53.420
<i>She's so easy!</i>

01:53.760 --> 01:57.780
Very well, then. I won't have it killed.

01:57.780 --> 02:00.890
But in return, you must 
teach it proper discipline.

02:00.890 --> 02:03.950
Thank you, kind Miss Claire!

02:03.950 --> 02:07.650
Also, don't be sneaky and hide it. 
Show it to everyone.

02:07.650 --> 02:08.560
Sure!

02:08.560 --> 02:11.510
And don't call it "Ralaire."

02:11.510 --> 02:13.350
Come up with a different name.

02:13.350 --> 02:15.750
Oh, it's too late for that.

02:15.750 --> 02:16.690
Too late?

02:16.690 --> 02:22.190
Well, you see, once you give 
a familiar a name, it never forgets it.

02:20.700 --> 02:22.830
<b></b>Ralaire

02:22.830 --> 02:25.950
So once again, it's great 
to know you, Ralaire!

02:25.950 --> 02:29.000
I object! I vehemently object!

03:59.000 --> 04:04.010
<b>Episode 5</b>

03:59.000 --> 04:04.010
<b>The Knight Exam Is Packed with Drama</b>

04:04.010 --> 04:06.010
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

04:04.010 --> 04:06.010
<b>Academy Knights Entry Exam 
Written Exam Results</b>

04:07.540 --> 04:10.170
I passed! I got in!

04:10.170 --> 04:13.420
So did I, Miss Claire! We're together!

04:13.420 --> 04:15.640
And congratulations, Misha!

04:15.640 --> 04:16.900
You are too kind.

04:16.900 --> 04:19.650
Miss Claire! You're ignoring me?!

04:20.180 --> 04:22.820
I can't get enough of 
that cold attitude, though!

04:22.820 --> 04:24.660
Why must you react that way?!

04:24.660 --> 04:26.410
So you girls got in, too?

04:30.220 --> 04:32.630
Well, I hear the written exam 
is just the first step.

04:32.630 --> 04:35.870
The real test is the practical 
exam that comes next.

04:35.870 --> 04:39.910
<i>The Academy Knights are an autonomous 
organization within the academy.</i>

04:39.910 --> 04:42.010
<i>They're basically the student council.</i>

04:42.550 --> 04:46.970
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

04:42.550 --> 04:46.970
<b>Written Exam Results</b>

04:42.550 --> 04:46.970
<b>1st
2nd
3rd
4th
5th
6th</b>

04:42.550 --> 04:46.970
<b>Rod Bauer
Yu Bauer
Claire François
Rae Taylor
Misha Jur
Thane Bauer</b>

04:42.550 --> 04:49.260
<i>But only the elite few who pass 
the rigorous entry exam can get in.</i>

04:49.260 --> 04:51.950
You took the exam, too, Misha?

04:51.950 --> 04:55.220
I had no idea you were interested 
in the Academy Knights.

04:55.220 --> 04:59.430
Miss Claire asked me to. 
She said Rae needed a guardian.

05:00.280 --> 05:01.280
That makes sense.

05:05.230 --> 05:07.210
Commoner, I'm issuing
a challenge.

05:07.210 --> 05:10.920
If you fail the knight exam, 
you will leave this academy.

05:10.920 --> 05:12.550
Huh? No, I won't.

05:12.550 --> 05:15.250
Would you at least give it 
a <i>little</i> consideration?

05:15.650 --> 05:18.370
Oh, fine, if you say so.

05:18.370 --> 05:21.630
Why don't we compete under 
the same terms as last time, then?

05:21.630 --> 05:23.270
Wait just a minute!

05:23.270 --> 05:25.510
You're going to trick me again, aren't you?

05:25.890 --> 05:28.140
Oh, poo! You remembered that?

05:28.490 --> 05:31.490
In that case, if I fail, you win,

05:31.490 --> 05:34.390
and if I pass, I win. How about that?

05:34.390 --> 05:38.520
Can't we say that if I pass, I win?

05:38.520 --> 05:40.830
That puts me at too great a disadvantage.

05:40.830 --> 05:43.340
We both know you're going to pass.

05:43.340 --> 05:46.110
Hmph. You really do get it.

05:46.550 --> 05:48.490
And if you win?

05:48.930 --> 05:53.260
Same as before. You have 
to do one thing I say.

05:56.190 --> 05:58.470
Ralaire! You can't come out of there!

05:58.470 --> 06:01.210
Oh, so that's the familiar 
I keep hearing about?

06:01.210 --> 06:03.020
It's cute.

06:04.530 --> 06:06.590
All of you who passed the written exam!

06:07.100 --> 06:09.400
That's Lorek, captain of the Academy Knights.

06:09.400 --> 06:11.850
That other guy's the vice captain.

06:12.320 --> 06:14.330
We'll need you to start moving right away.

06:14.330 --> 06:16.480
The practical exam will take 
place on the athletic ground.

06:24.270 --> 06:26.740
In the entry exam for 
the honorable Academy Knights,

06:26.740 --> 06:29.610
the main event is 
the one-on-one mock battles!

06:30.530 --> 06:31.960
There will be ten battles.

06:31.960 --> 06:34.740
The most highly anticipated 
battles based on survey responses

06:35.140 --> 06:38.750
are the first battle, 
Thane Bauer versus Yu Bauer...

06:39.350 --> 06:42.750
the sixth battle, 
Rod Bauer versus Misha Jur...

06:43.290 --> 06:47.010
and the tenth battle, 
Claire François versus Rae Taylor!

06:54.320 --> 06:58.020
The battles will take place within 
this barrier that reduces damage taken.

06:58.020 --> 07:02.510
So you can fight with all your 
strength and no reservations!

07:03.010 --> 07:06.530
Now, combatants for 
the first battle, step forward!

07:10.630 --> 07:13.280
Go easy on me, okay, Brother?

07:13.280 --> 07:14.850
Prince Thane...

07:14.850 --> 07:16.020
Prince Yu...

07:16.020 --> 07:19.290
We get two princes right 
from the start? What a show.

07:19.290 --> 07:21.300
Combatants, ready...

07:21.300 --> 07:22.230
Begin!

07:30.130 --> 07:32.710
And Prince Thane is 
immediately on the offensive!

07:32.710 --> 07:34.890
Prince Thane is an advanced 
user of wind magic.

07:35.330 --> 07:37.830
Wind magic is primarily used for support,

07:37.830 --> 07:42.160
but he uses it to boost his physical 
strength in the style of a magic warrior.

07:47.140 --> 07:50.030
Don't be so impatient, Brother.

07:50.030 --> 07:55.440
What if you hurt your precious baby 
brother by being in such a hurry?

07:56.360 --> 07:57.580
Keep talking!

07:59.110 --> 08:00.120
Water!

08:03.790 --> 08:06.260
Prince Yu is good.

08:06.260 --> 08:08.550
He's using water to turn 
all his attacks aside.

08:10.560 --> 08:13.100
Unfortunately for you, 
I'm a long-distance fighter.

08:17.470 --> 08:19.850
Anyone fighting on that would slip.

08:19.850 --> 08:22.600
Which puts Prince Thane, 
a close-range fighter, at a disadvantage.

08:22.600 --> 08:26.750
Now, I guess it's time for my counterattack.

08:27.890 --> 08:30.190
Prince Yu is an intermediate 
water magic user.

08:30.190 --> 08:32.740
When you see him use ice 
magic as cleverly as this,

08:32.740 --> 08:35.490
he's the very image of a prince of ice!

08:37.990 --> 08:38.870
Go!

08:39.870 --> 08:40.830
Prince Thane!

08:46.000 --> 08:49.000
His wall of wind is deflecting the icicles!

08:49.000 --> 08:51.510
And now Prince Thane is 
charging straight for him!

08:51.510 --> 08:53.460
But beneath his feet is ice!

08:54.210 --> 08:56.220
He's hardening air to step on!

08:56.220 --> 08:57.760
Yikes...

08:57.760 --> 08:58.720
Not.

09:00.780 --> 09:02.220
Ice Pillar!

09:05.730 --> 09:08.950
Prince Thane is trapped 
within pillars of ice!

09:08.950 --> 09:11.610
His wall of wind can't deflect that!

09:15.470 --> 09:16.740
<i>The shards are blocking my...</i>

09:21.950 --> 09:23.240
I give.

09:23.860 --> 09:25.750
The first battle is over!

09:26.200 --> 09:28.500
The winner is Prince Thane!

09:28.500 --> 09:31.610
You're definitely strong, Thane.

09:31.610 --> 09:34.650
And you weren't really 
giving it your all, were you?

09:34.650 --> 09:37.510
You even saved your healing magic.

09:37.510 --> 09:40.020
Prince Thane is so amazing!

09:40.020 --> 09:42.210
<i>That's a fantasy battle for you!</i>

09:42.930 --> 09:44.220
Go for it!

09:44.220 --> 09:45.970
You can do it!

09:44.730 --> 09:47.520
Next up is the sixth battle!

09:47.520 --> 09:49.460
Good luck, Misha!

09:51.210 --> 09:52.780
I'm not looking forward to this.

09:53.720 --> 09:56.240
Oh, dear. She isn't very 
enthusiastic about this.

09:56.240 --> 09:57.900
Well, of course not.

09:58.300 --> 10:02.030
She's up against Prince Rod, after all.

10:02.030 --> 10:03.660
Misha Jur, eh?

10:04.060 --> 10:07.160
You don't need to hold back against me. 
Give it all you've got.

10:07.540 --> 10:09.950
Thank you for this opportunity 
to practice against you.

10:09.950 --> 10:12.160
Seriously, you can stop being so...

10:12.560 --> 10:13.670
Whatever.

10:14.060 --> 10:17.670
I'll make you go all-out 
by force if I have to!

10:18.030 --> 10:19.080
Come!

10:22.930 --> 10:25.390
This is how I fight!

10:25.390 --> 10:28.940
My army of flames—my Minions!

10:31.060 --> 10:32.550
There are so many...

10:32.550 --> 10:33.570
Sure are!

10:33.570 --> 10:34.940
Go!

10:35.310 --> 10:37.330
The Minions are attacking!

10:37.330 --> 10:40.620
Things are looking dire for Misha now!

10:46.800 --> 10:48.080
<i>Was that sound...</i>

10:48.080 --> 10:50.580
Whoa! What in the world was that?!

10:50.580 --> 10:53.090
All the Minions disappeared!

10:53.090 --> 10:56.400
Did you hear that strange noise?

10:56.400 --> 10:58.550
Like fingernails on a chalkboard...

10:59.860 --> 11:02.440
Misha's wind magic is an offensive type

11:02.440 --> 11:05.350
that channels her magic 
into sound to attack a target.

11:05.350 --> 11:07.850
It's called "Siren."

11:07.850 --> 11:10.780
I see. In that case...

11:10.780 --> 11:12.320
How about this?!

11:13.730 --> 11:14.730
Go!

11:20.610 --> 11:21.610
Burst!

11:23.890 --> 11:25.850
What immense firepower!

11:25.850 --> 11:28.300
Surely there's nothing she can do about this!

11:28.300 --> 11:29.290
Misha!

11:30.600 --> 11:33.670
Amazing! Misha is unharmed!

11:34.670 --> 11:37.170
Was that wind magic, too?

11:37.170 --> 11:39.670
Yes, it was Vacuum Rupture.

11:39.670 --> 11:48.180
<b>Flask
Exterior</b>

11:39.670 --> 11:48.180
<b>Vacuum</b>

11:39.670 --> 11:48.180
<b>Flask
Interior</b>

11:40.150 --> 11:45.220
<i>She creates gaps in the space 
around her to shut out heat.</i>

11:45.220 --> 11:48.180
<i>It's the same principle as a vacuum flask.</i>

11:49.680 --> 11:50.850
Interesting.

11:50.850 --> 11:53.810
You're a lot more interesting 
than I expected!

11:55.510 --> 11:56.420
Go!

12:05.780 --> 12:08.500
Prince Rod unleashes a barrage of attacks!

12:09.670 --> 12:12.800
Rod really never changes, does he?

12:12.800 --> 12:14.250
He never runs out of
magic power.

12:14.250 --> 12:17.920
Prince Rod's aptitude for fire 
magic is only intermediate,

12:17.920 --> 12:20.340
but he has an exceptional 
amount of magic power.

12:20.710 --> 12:24.240
Still, isn't he taking this a bit too far?

12:24.240 --> 12:26.680
Yes, but pretty soon...

12:33.690 --> 12:35.340
I give.

12:35.340 --> 12:36.860
Th-That's it!

12:37.210 --> 12:38.480
Misha!

12:42.530 --> 12:44.030
What's wrong with Misha?!

12:44.430 --> 12:45.710
She's oxygen-deficient.

12:45.710 --> 12:47.020
She's what?!

12:47.550 --> 12:51.570
Prince Rod's nonstop attacks and her 
continuous use of Vacuum Rupture

12:51.570 --> 12:54.540
took all the oxygen out of her.

12:54.900 --> 12:59.330
To put it simply, she was overwhelmed by 
the sheer volume of magic he threw at her.

13:00.970 --> 13:02.660
Misha, are you okay?

13:03.460 --> 13:05.680
I'm fine, Prince Yu.

13:07.990 --> 13:09.780
You went too far, Brother.

13:09.780 --> 13:10.930
Did I?

13:11.340 --> 13:13.480
Should we take her to the nurse's office?

13:27.110 --> 13:31.210
This knight exam has already been far 
more exciting than those of years past,

13:31.210 --> 13:32.700
and now it's reached the final battle!

13:32.700 --> 13:35.500
Miss Claire! You can do it!

13:35.500 --> 13:37.500
Go get her!

13:37.820 --> 13:40.500
I think we're gonna get 
a pretty good show here.

13:40.820 --> 13:42.150
Combatants, step forward!

13:43.260 --> 13:45.000
The tenth battle...

13:45.000 --> 13:47.010
Claire François versus

13:47.530 --> 13:49.020
Rae Taylor!

13:55.020 --> 13:57.890
Prepare yourself, Rae Taylor!

13:57.890 --> 14:01.520
I will personally read you your last rites!

14:01.840 --> 14:05.030
Sure! Let's have lots of fun, Miss Claire!

14:05.490 --> 14:07.100
Did you say "fun"?

14:07.580 --> 14:12.280
A mere commoner shouldn't think 
she can defeat me so easily!

14:12.280 --> 14:15.840
Now, the final battle will... begin!

14:22.210 --> 14:25.210
What's this? Neither combatant is moving!

14:25.210 --> 14:28.830
Aren't you going to attack? 
This isn't much of a contest!

14:28.830 --> 14:32.470
I'm happy just standing here 
looking at you, Miss Claire.

14:33.240 --> 14:35.720
You're making fun of me again!

14:35.720 --> 14:39.480
But if you really insist...

14:39.480 --> 14:40.820
I'll start!

14:44.820 --> 14:48.800
Rae's rock wall has surrounded Claire!

14:48.800 --> 14:50.820
She's putting her barrier to use.

14:50.820 --> 14:52.740
Hmph! This is nothing!

14:57.950 --> 15:00.280
She broke the rock? No...

15:00.280 --> 15:02.130
The rock is melting away!

15:02.130 --> 15:05.130
Wow, that's some firepower.

15:05.130 --> 15:07.700
The fire attribute is strong against earth,

15:07.700 --> 15:10.630
but still, I didn't know it could melt it.

15:10.630 --> 15:12.800
Then let me pick on you even more.

15:18.890 --> 15:20.410
That won't work!

15:24.400 --> 15:26.930
Is that a flame barrier?!

15:26.930 --> 15:29.320
Since flames don't have a physical body,

15:29.320 --> 15:31.360
a wall of them isn't usually 
effective at defense,

15:31.720 --> 15:36.280
but if the flames are hot enough to melt 
the stone instantly, that changes everything.

15:36.730 --> 15:40.070
Her style of controlling 
and freely manipulating fire

15:40.070 --> 15:43.670
is why Miss Claire is known 
as the "Red Lotus Queen."

15:44.290 --> 15:46.800
I'll make my own move now!

15:46.800 --> 15:50.940
When you're a noble, even 
your magic must be artistic!

15:50.940 --> 15:52.800
Flames, roar forth!

15:53.890 --> 15:55.300
Flame Lance, huh?

15:55.300 --> 15:57.040
That's my Miss Claire!

15:57.040 --> 16:00.140
Sensibilities aside, you have such 
a high level of control capacity!

16:00.140 --> 16:01.600
Quiet!

16:03.850 --> 16:06.360
Sorry, but I can't do that!

16:10.030 --> 16:14.110
You fool! Have you already forgotten 
how I melted your earth previously?

16:16.620 --> 16:18.490
Wha... How?!

16:18.860 --> 16:22.120
Looks like it's made of a different 
material than the last one.

16:22.120 --> 16:24.950
What in the world could it be composed of?

16:24.950 --> 16:26.780
<i>Tungsten carbide.</i>

16:26.780 --> 16:29.450
<i>It's about twice as strong as steel,</i>

16:29.450 --> 16:32.470
<i>and its melting point is over 2,000 degrees.</i>

16:32.470 --> 16:35.970
<i>I'm putting my knowledge 
from my previous life to use.</i>

16:36.350 --> 16:37.770
I get it.

16:37.770 --> 16:40.970
You may be rotten, but your 
aptitude is still exceptional.

16:40.970 --> 16:44.350
But I have plenty of ways to deal with this.

16:45.850 --> 16:48.820
Claire is using Flame Lance once again!

16:48.820 --> 16:52.110
But this one is drastically bigger!

16:52.110 --> 16:53.860
Time to finish this!

16:56.710 --> 16:58.120
It got around her!

16:58.120 --> 16:59.830
Now, burst!

17:00.830 --> 17:03.190
The Flame Lance turned 
into a Fireball fusillade!

17:03.190 --> 17:05.470
What a remarkable control technique!

17:07.950 --> 17:09.300
Wha—

17:09.300 --> 17:11.370
She shot all of them down!

17:11.370 --> 17:13.550
Rae is still putting up a good fight!

17:13.550 --> 17:17.120
Whoa, she got to them 
all in time from there?

17:17.120 --> 17:18.590
It does seem odd.

17:18.590 --> 17:22.680
As though she's already familiar 
with Claire's combat style.

17:22.680 --> 17:25.560
Huh? Oh, you know why that is.

17:25.560 --> 17:29.560
Because she's always 
thinking about Miss Claire!

17:29.560 --> 17:32.640
<i>I mean, frankly, they're right.</i>

17:32.640 --> 17:36.570
<i>I've memorized every last detail 
of Miss Claire's combat style.</i>

17:38.130 --> 17:39.630
A mere commoner...

17:39.630 --> 17:42.760
Oh? What's the matter? Finished already?

17:42.760 --> 17:43.500
Of course not!

17:44.120 --> 17:45.930
Forgive me, Prince Rod.

17:50.810 --> 17:54.340
I get it. She's copying your Minions.

17:54.750 --> 17:55.880
Go!

17:57.030 --> 18:00.060
Rae fights back with her wall, but now...

18:02.350 --> 18:04.750
Well, I don't mind if she copies it,

18:04.750 --> 18:08.370
but Claire doesn't have the magic 
power to keep that up for long.

18:08.370 --> 18:10.480
I'm sure she doesn't care.

18:10.820 --> 18:13.110
She's probably trying 
to deprive her of oxygen.

18:13.110 --> 18:15.560
If you're trying to cut off someone's air,

18:15.560 --> 18:17.520
it doesn't have to take that long.

18:17.870 --> 18:20.370
Rae continues to focus on defense!

18:22.580 --> 18:24.310
Take this, then!

18:24.740 --> 18:27.460
Ah! Now Rae is fighting back!

18:27.460 --> 18:29.540
If she gets trapped in there, she's done!

18:31.110 --> 18:33.550
<i>I won't fall for the same trick twice!</i>

18:35.550 --> 18:39.070
<i>Ooh! Miss Claire looks so 
cool doing mid-air flips!</i>

18:39.070 --> 18:42.930
<i>Truly a lady who excels at both 
academics and athletics! I love you!</i>

18:42.930 --> 18:46.930
What are you going to 
show me next, Miss Claire?

18:46.930 --> 18:51.190
Impudent little... Don't you get cocky now!

18:51.190 --> 18:55.530
I never thought I'd have to 
use this against a commoner.

18:55.530 --> 18:56.780
Light!

19:00.780 --> 19:03.420
<i>That's the François family crest...</i>

19:03.780 --> 19:05.370
Magic Ray!

19:14.030 --> 19:15.960
That was a warning shot.

19:16.340 --> 19:20.850
As you've seen, it's exponentially more 
powerful than the magic I previously used.

19:20.850 --> 19:24.350
Even I can't use it too many times.

19:24.750 --> 19:26.660
If you get it now, then surrender.

19:26.660 --> 19:30.060
It's true that I could never 
dodge that once I see it starting.

19:30.060 --> 19:31.550
That's right!

19:31.550 --> 19:32.620
But...

19:33.360 --> 19:36.220
I still can't stand to lose, 
so I'll try to win.

19:40.980 --> 19:42.600
Miss Claire!

19:42.600 --> 19:45.790
Come on! Of all the spells you could use, 
you pick a dull one like—

19:45.790 --> 19:47.950
And here's even more.

19:48.650 --> 19:51.460
I have to fall even farther?!

19:53.140 --> 19:56.120
Miss Claire! Can you get out?

19:56.120 --> 19:57.460
Grr!

19:57.460 --> 19:59.950
Stay right where you are!

19:59.950 --> 20:02.670
Just wait! I'll widen this hole with magic!

20:02.670 --> 20:03.970
Give it up, Claire.

20:04.790 --> 20:06.220
Prince Thane!

20:06.220 --> 20:09.510
Wh-What are you saying? I can still—

20:09.510 --> 20:10.870
Did you forget

20:10.870 --> 20:13.220
that Rae is a dual caster?

20:14.390 --> 20:16.940
She hasn't even used her water magic,

20:16.940 --> 20:19.730
and it's a lot more 
effective against your fire.

20:19.730 --> 20:22.230
You've been holding back all this time?!

20:22.230 --> 20:23.200
Yep!

20:24.530 --> 20:26.000
<i>You mock me?!</i>

20:26.000 --> 20:27.200
Stop!

20:27.660 --> 20:32.480
Miss Claire, I'm sorry, 
but I must call a referee stop.

20:34.080 --> 20:36.710
The winner is Rae!

20:36.710 --> 20:39.530
You fought so well, Miss Claire!

20:39.530 --> 20:41.710
You were so brave!

20:42.780 --> 20:46.720
The results of the entry exam will 
be posted on the bulletin board.

20:47.150 --> 20:49.220
Make sure you check for yourselves.

20:49.990 --> 20:50.920
What?

20:51.220 --> 20:55.050
The ones who passed were Prince Rod, 
Prince Yu, Prince Thane,

20:55.050 --> 20:56.980
the commoner, Misha...

20:56.980 --> 20:58.360
and me?!

20:58.920 --> 21:01.730
Oh, did I forget to tell you?

21:02.210 --> 21:05.300
What counts in the practical 
exam is raw ability.

21:05.300 --> 21:07.990
Whether you win or lose 
has no bearing on the result.

21:07.990 --> 21:09.330
You're kidding!

21:09.330 --> 21:15.000
So I'll be looking forward to working 
with you, Miss Claire and Rae Taylor!

21:17.070 --> 21:20.500
Miss Claire...

21:21.100 --> 21:23.770
I know, I know! We made a deal, right?!

21:23.770 --> 21:25.570
Tell me what you want me to do!

21:25.570 --> 21:27.390
Okay! Then...

21:28.610 --> 21:31.760
No matter what happens, don't give up.

21:33.520 --> 21:36.050
Excuse me? What's the meaning of this?

21:36.050 --> 21:38.580
That's the same thing you said last time.

21:38.580 --> 21:40.510
I know. That's fine.

21:40.510 --> 21:42.760
Make the same promise to me again.

21:43.270 --> 21:46.170
W-Well, I suppose that's fine...

21:47.300 --> 21:52.610
I, Claire François, swear to God 
that I will never give up.

21:52.610 --> 21:55.410
No matter what happens, 
I will not abandon hope.

21:55.410 --> 21:58.330
I swear to continue fighting 
until the very end.

22:01.010 --> 22:02.920
Are you sure that's all you want?

22:02.920 --> 22:04.120
Yes!

22:04.810 --> 22:08.300
Wait... I have a feeling 
I'm forgetting something...

22:12.630 --> 22:14.530
What do I do with this?

23:46.550 --> 23:50.550
Miss Claire, Rae, congratulations 
on getting into the Knights!

23:50.550 --> 23:53.740
Um, about that... 
One of the knights is actually...

23:53.740 --> 23:56.220
Now we'll be together in 
the Knights, too, Miss Claire!

23:56.220 --> 23:58.370
I'll have to speak directly to Captain Lorek!

23:58.370 --> 24:00.520
U-Um...

23:59.540 --> 24:01.040
<b>Episode 6</b>

23:59.540 --> 24:01.040
<b>The Secret Reason Must Not Be Told to Anyone</b>
